      "text": "To find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 12 and 20, we use the Euclidean algorithm, which involves repeated division.\n\n1. Divide the larger number (20) by the smaller number (12) and find the remainder.\n\\[ 20 \\div 12 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 8 \\]\n\n2. Replace the larger number (20) with the smaller number (12) and the smaller number with the remainder (8), then repeat the process.\n\\[ 12 \\div 8 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 4 \\]\n\n3. Continue the process.\n\\[ 8 \\div 4 = 2 \\text{ remainder } 0 \\]\n\nSince we have reached a remainder of 0, the divisor at this step (4) is the greatest common divisor of 12 and 20.\n\nThus, the greatest common divisor of 12 and 20 is \\(\\boxed{4}\\).",
