      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 12 and 20, we can use the Euclidean algorithm. Here are the steps:\n\n1. Divide the larger number (20) by the smaller number (12) and find the remainder.\n   \\[\n   20 \\div 12 = 1 \\quad \\text{with a remainder of} \\quad 8\n   \\]\n   So, we have:\n   \\[\n   20 = 12 \\cdot 1 + 8\n   \\]\n\n2. Now, take the smaller number (12) and divide it by the remainder (8) from the previous step.\n   \\[\n   12 \\div 8 = 1 \\quad \\text{with a remainder of} \\quad 4\n   \\]\n   So, we have:\n   \\[\n   12 = 8 \\cdot 1 + 4\n   \\]\n\n3. Next, take the previous divisor (8) and divide it by the remainder (4) from the previous step.\n   \\[\n   8 \\div 4 = 2 \\quad \\text{with a remainder of} \\quad 0\n   \\]\n   So, we have:\n   \\[\n   8 = 4 \\cdot 2 + 0\n   \\]\n\nSince the remainder is now 0, the divisor at this step, which is 4, is the greatest common divisor of 12 and 20.\n\nTherefore, the greatest common divisor of 12 and 20 is \\boxed{4}.",
