    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 12 and 20, we can use the prime factorization method. Here are the steps:\n\n1. **Find the prime factorization of each number:**\n   - The prime factorization of 12 is:\n     \\[\n     12 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 3 = 2^2 \\times 3\n     \\]\n   - The prime factorization of 20 is:\n     \\[\n     20 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 5 = 2^2 \\times 5\n     \\]\n\n2. **Identify the common prime factors:**\n   - The prime factors of 12 are \\(2^2 \\times 3\\).\n   - The prime factors of 20 are \\(2^2 \\times 5\\).\n   - The common prime factor is \\(2^2\\).\n\n3. **Determine the lowest power of the common prime factor:**\n   - The lowest power of 2 that appears in both factorizations is \\(2^2\\).\n\n4. **Multiply the lowest powers of the common prime factors:**\n   - Therefore, the GCD is:\n     \\[\n     2^2 = 4\n     \\]\n\nSo, the greatest common divisor of 12 and 20 is \\(\\boxed{4}\\).",
